| `test_quality.realness.exempt.<test>` | string | none in keel or a generated project; absent, `{}`, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.realness.exempt = {}` | a test's function-level pytest node id, `<path>.py::<name>` or `<path>.py::<Class>::<name>`, mapped to a non-blank reason | `tests/realness.py` (`policy`, `verdict`), called by `tests/integration/test_realness_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `test_quality.realness.exempt` row | Lets the named test through the realness gate though it replaces a dependency with a mock: for a test whose dependency cannot run in the suite. An entry whose test is not `mock`, or that names no test, is stale and fails the gate. A value the loader refuses raises `ConfigError` naming this key. | a test that can drive the real part, a fake or the app in process: drive it | always |
